var e="Also describe separately the possible short-term effects (hours to days) and medium-term effects (weeks to months) on those involved, service delivery and decision-making. Identify at least two plausible game changers: for each, state the condition under which the scenario could change course and its possible consequence, without treating the selected factor values as facts that can be changed. Distinguish established consequences, assumptions and conditional developments. Place the two requested reflection or exercise questions at the end.",i=[{id:"evenementenveiligheid",label:"Event safety",desc:`A four-layer exercise kit covering event characteristics, disruptions, measures and effects. Combine them to discuss assumptions about visitors, access, capacity, decision-making and recovery. Expected attendance may deliberately exceed permitted capacity: that very mismatch can be a relevant dilemma.

Source: [NIPV – Event safety](https://nipv.nl/onderzoek/evenementenveiligheid/).`,categories:[{id:"evenement",label:"Event characteristics",desc:"Type, location, scale, duration and visitor mix define the starting situation",factors:[{id:"soort",label:"Type of event",desc:"What gathering provides the setting for the exercise?",values:[["festival","Cultural festival"],["wedstrijd","Sports match"],["markt","Public market"]]},{id:"terrein",label:"Venue",desc:"How is the public space physically arranged?",values:[["openbaar","Open public space"],["afgesloten","Enclosed site"],["gebouw","Building or hall"]]},{id:"opkomst",label:"Expected attendance",desc:"How many visitors might arrive at the venue at the same time? This may exceed permitted capacity.",values:[["klein","Up to 500 visitors"],["middel","1,000–5,000 visitors"],["groot","More than 10,000 visitors"]]},{id:"duur",label:"Event duration",desc:"For how long must the organiser deploy people and resources?",values:[["kort","Several hours"],["dag","A full day"],["meerdaags","Several consecutive days"]]},{id:"moment",label:"Time frame",desc:"When does the gathering take place?",values:[["dag","A single part of the day"],["avond","One evening only"],["doorlopend","Continuously over several days"]]},{id:"bezoekers",label:"Visitor mix",desc:"What needs relating to information, mobility and facilities deserve attention without assigning people a risk profile?",values:[["families","Many families"],["gemengd","Mixed audience"],["ondersteuning","Many visitors with support needs"]]}]},{id:"belasting",label:"Disruptions and pressures",desc:"Weather, accessibility, incidents or crowd pressure can change how events unfold.",factors:[{id:"weer",label:"Weather conditions",desc:"What conditions should be taken into account in preparations?",values:[["rustig","Calm weather"],["hitte","Persistent heat"],["regen","Prolonged rain"],["storm","Strong winds"]]},{id:"bereik",label:"Access to the surrounding area",desc:"How accessible are the usual arrival and departure routes for visitors and emergency services?",values:[["normaal","Normal access"],["beperkt","Some delays"],["dicht","Usual arrival route unavailable"]]},{id:"medisch",label:"Medical assistance needs",desc:"What level of medical incidents has been confirmed at this gathering?",values:[["geen","No injuries"],["beperkt","A few minor injuries"],["ernstig","Serious injuries"]]},{id:"techniek",label:"Available visitor communications",desc:"Which communication facilities currently work?",values:[["volledig","Public-address system and mobile channels available"],["mobiel","Only mobile channels available"],["terplekke","Only verbal communication by staff"]]},{id:"stroom",label:"Visitor flow",desc:"When is the greatest simultaneous pressure felt at the venue or in the surrounding area?",values:[["gespreid","Evenly distributed"],["entree","Peak on arrival"],["vertrek","Peak on departure"]]}]},{id:"organisatie",label:"Measures and organisation",desc:"Access arrangements, facilities and coordination provide options for action.",factors:[{id:"maximum",label:"Permitted simultaneous capacity",desc:"What limit has been set for this fictional venue?",values:[["vijfhonderd","Maximum 500"],["vijfduizend","Maximum 5,000"],["ruim","More than 10,000"]]},{id:"toegang",label:"Admission arrangements",desc:"How are visitors admitted?",values:[["vrij","Open admission"],["ticket","Ticketed admission"],["uitnodiging","Invitation only"]]},{id:"zorg",label:"Medical preparedness",desc:"What first-aid provision has been planned for visitors?",values:[["basis","Basic on-site provision"],["meervoud","Multiple first-aid stations"],["opschalen","Scalable medical support"]]},{id:"regie",label:"Coordination model",desc:"Who coordinates decisions among the organiser, municipality and emergency services?",values:[["organisator","Organiser with designated contacts"],["gezamenlijk","Joint coordination meeting"],["crisis","Escalated public crisis-management structure"]]},{id:"bericht",label:"Active communication channel",desc:"How does the organiser reach visitors during this situation?",values:[["omroep","Public-address system"],["mobiel","Mobile messages"],["medewerkers","Staff on site"]]},{id:"opvang",label:"Support after an interruption",desc:"What arrangements are in place if visitors cannot continue?",values:[["terrein","Temporary place on site"],["omgeving","Shelter in the surrounding area"],["regionaal","Coordination of regional shelter"]]}]},{id:"gevolgen",label:"Effects and recovery",desc:"Consequences for people, the programme, the surrounding area and the organiser inform the evaluation.",factors:[{id:"gezondheid",label:"Effects on visitors",desc:"What health effects have actually been confirmed, rather than merely feared?",values:[["geen","No one injured"],["licht","Minor injuries"],["ernstig","Serious injuries"]]},{id:"uitloop",label:"Effects on the programme",desc:"How does the situation alter the planned programme?",values:[["opplan","As planned"],["vertraging","Temporary delay"],["stop","Early termination"]]},{id:"omgeving",label:"Effects on local residents",desc:"What do people immediately around the event experience?",values:[["beperkt","Limited disruption"],["bereik","Access under pressure"],["voorziening","Temporary loss of services"]]},{id:"vertrouwen",label:"Public information needs",desc:"How much demand is there for reliable explanation and accountability?",values:[["lokaal","Mainly visitors and local residents"],["regionaal","Regional interest as well"],["breed","Widespread public interest"]]},{id:"evaluatie",label:"Follow-up after the event",desc:"What aftercare or learning activity does this exercise situation call for?",values:[["regulier","Routine evaluation"],["nazorg","Aftercare and follow-up"],["onderzoek","Joint fact-finding"]]}]}],exclusions:[["duur.meerdaags","moment.dag"],["duur.meerdaags","moment.avond"],["duur.kort","moment.doorlopend"],["duur.dag","moment.doorlopend"],["techniek.mobiel","bericht.omroep"],["techniek.terplekke","bericht.omroep"],["techniek.terplekke","bericht.mobiel"],["medisch.geen","gezondheid.licht"],["medisch.geen","gezondheid.ernstig"],["medisch.beperkt","gezondheid.geen"],["medisch.ernstig","gezondheid.geen"],["medisch.ernstig","gezondheid.licht"]],template:`The gathering is {1} and the venue is {2}, with expected attendance of {3}. Its duration is {4}, its time frame is {5}, and the audience is {6}.
The weather is {7} and access to the surrounding area is {8}. The picture regarding medical incidents is {9}; visitor communications are {10}, while visitor flows are characterised by {11}.
Permitted capacity is {12} and admission is {13}. Medical preparedness consists of {14}; decisions are coordinated through {15}, visitors receive information through {16}, and {17} is arranged in case of interruption.
For visitors, the health effects are {18}. The effect on the programme is {19}; for local residents this means {20}, and public information needs are {21}. Afterwards, {22} follows.`,prompt:"Write a credible event-safety exercise scenario in English using all selected values. Structure the narrative around the lead-up, disruption, measures and effects. Describe visitor flows, cooperation among the organiser, municipality and emergency services, and a dilemma involving access, capacity, information or weather. Distinguish expected attendance from permitted capacity: exceeding capacity is a potential problem, not an impossible combination. Make assumptions explicit; do not provide operational vulnerabilities or instructions for bypassing safeguards. End with two reflection questions.",example:{label:"A festival evening takes an unexpected turn",desc:"<p>A cultural festival at an enclosed site expects several thousand visitors for an evening programme. Heat and delayed access cause a sudden surge of arrivals at the entrance. A few visitors need minor medical attention. The organiser temporarily pauses the programme and informs the audience over the public-address system.</p><p>At a joint meeting, the municipality and emergency services consider how permitted capacity, shelter in the surrounding area and access for local residents affect one another. The following morning brings aftercare and an evaluation of the decision and the communication.</p>",choices:["soort.festival","terrein.afgesloten","opkomst.middel","duur.kort","moment.avond","bezoekers.gemengd","weer.hitte","bereik.beperkt","medisch.beperkt","techniek.volledig","stroom.entree","maximum.vijfduizend","toegang.ticket","zorg.meervoud","regie.gezamenlijk","bericht.omroep","opvang.omgeving","gezondheid.licht","uitloop.vertraging","omgeving.bereik","vertrouwen.regionaal","evaluatie.nazorg"]}},{id:"cybercontinuiteit",label:"Cyber incident and continuity",desc:`A defensive exercise model for service delivery, detection, interdependencies, decision-making and recovery after a digital incident. The focus is on continuity of governance and services, not attack techniques.

Source: [NCSC – Incidents and recovery](https://www.ncsc.nl/incidenten-en-herstellen/resultaten).`,categories:[{id:"dienst",label:"Service delivery",desc:"Which service and digital dependencies are central?",factors:[{id:"sector",label:"Affected service",desc:"What public or societal function is affected by the disruption?",values:[["zorg","Healthcare"],["gemeente","Municipal services"],["logistiek","Logistics coordination"]]},{id:"netwerk",label:"Service network connection",desc:"To what extent is the service connected to external networks?",values:[["los","Fully standalone without a network"],["partner","Partner network only"],["internet","Accessible via the internet"]]},{id:"afhankelijkheid",label:"Critical dependency",desc:"Which internal or external link is needed for the service to function?",values:[["intern","In-house IT organisation"],["leverancier","External supplier"],["meervoud","Multiple partner organisations"]]},{id:"gebruikers",label:"Service users",desc:"Which group experiences the effects of the disruption first?",values:[["medewerkers","Internal staff"],["inwoners","Residents and clients"],["keten","Partner organisations"]]}]},{id:"incident",label:"Incident picture",desc:"The observable effect and the stage of the response.",factors:[{id:"effect",label:"Observable effect",desc:"What does the organisation notice without having established the cause?",values:[["uitval","Complete outage of the digital service"],["twijfel","Uncertainty about data quality"],["leverancier","Disruption at a supplier"]]},{id:"fase",label:"Response stage",desc:"Where is the organisation in the incident cycle?",values:[["detectie","Detection and verification"],["respons","Coordination during the incident"],["herstel","Recovery and evaluation"]]},{id:"detectie",label:"Initial signal",desc:"What observation first brings the problem to light?",values:[["gebruikers","Reports from users"],["monitoring","Internal monitoring"],["partner","Alert from a partner organisation"]]},{id:"zekerheid",label:"Certainty about the cause",desc:"How confident is the assessment of the cause at this point?",values:[["onbekend","Cause unknown"],["werkhypothese","Working hypothesis under investigation"],["bevestigd","Cause confirmed by investigation"]]}]},{id:"aanpak",label:"Continuity and contact",desc:"How can services and communication continue?",factors:[{id:"kanaal",label:"Channel for this service",desc:"Through which channel can users access this service?",values:[["lokaal","In person only"],["intern","Via the internal network"],["online","Via a public online portal"]]},{id:"niveau",label:"Digital availability",desc:"To what extent is the affected digital service currently working?",values:[["offline","Not available digitally"],["beperkt","Partly available digitally"],["normaal","Normally available digitally"]]},{id:"noodproces",label:"Continuity process",desc:"What temporary procedure keeps essential services available?",values:[["handmatig","Manual registration"],["prioriteit","Priority requests only"],["alternatief","Separate alternative service"]]},{id:"gegevens",label:"Data status",desc:"What is known about the reliability of data for this service?",values:[["onzeker","Reliability still uncertain"],["controle","Rechecking in progress"],["geverifieerd","Reliability confirmed"]]}]},{id:"bestuur",label:"Decision-making and recovery",desc:"Ownership, cooperation, external communication and recovery are considered separately.",factors:[{id:"regie",label:"Decision-making lead",desc:"Where are priorities for service delivery and recovery set?",values:[["dienst","Within the service"],["organisatie","Organisation-wide crisis team"],["keten","Jointly with partner organisations"]]},{id:"afstemming",label:"Coordination with partners",desc:"How do the organisations involved exchange status information?",values:[["bilateraal","Individual contacts"],["gezamenlijk","Shared situational picture"],["tijdelijk","Temporary coordination meeting"]]},{id:"publiek",label:"Public communication",desc:"What can responsibly be communicated to users?",values:[["ontvangst","Report received; facts still unknown"],["dienst","Effects on service delivery known"],["herstel","Recovery steps confirmed"]]},{id:"herstel",label:"Recovery status",desc:"To what extent is the affected digital service usable again?",values:[["niet","Recovery not yet started"],["beperkt","Phased recovery"],["afgerond","Service fully restored"]]}]}],exclusions:[["netwerk.los","kanaal.intern"],["netwerk.los","kanaal.online"],["netwerk.partner","kanaal.online"],["effect.uitval","niveau.beperkt"],["effect.uitval","niveau.normaal"],["effect.uitval","herstel.afgerond"],["effect.twijfel","gegevens.geverifieerd"],["niveau.offline","herstel.afgerond"]],template:`The affected service is {1}, with a network connection of {2} and a critical dependency on {3}. The initial effects are felt by {4}.
The observable effect is {5}. The response is at the stage of {6}; the first signal is {7} and certainty about the cause is {8}.
The channel for the service is {9}, while digital availability is {10}. The temporary procedure is {11}; the status of the data is {12}.
Decisions are led by {13}, and coordination with partners takes the form of {14}. Communication to users is {15}; the recovery status is {16}.`,prompt:"Create an English-language defensive cyber-continuity exercise scenario based on all selected values. Organise it around the first signal, verification, consequences for users, governance and recovery. Bring out trade-offs concerning uncertainty, data quality, communication and partner organisations. A service that is down digitally may continue through a temporary contingency process; do not confuse the service with its underlying technology. Distinguish observations from suspicions; do not describe attack steps, vulnerabilities or ways around safeguards. End with two questions about service delivery and accountability.",example:{label:"The municipal portal goes offline",desc:"<p>Users report that a municipal online portal is no longer working. The organisation investigates with its supplier whether the existing data can still be trusted. A manual contingency process keeps priority requests possible, but requires additional explanation for residents.</p><p>The organisation-wide crisis team discusses with partner organisations how to share their situational picture. Digital recovery has not yet begun, so the initial public notice explains the effects on service delivery without naming an unconfirmed cause.</p>",choices:["sector.gemeente","netwerk.internet","afhankelijkheid.leverancier","gebruikers.inwoners","effect.uitval","fase.respons","detectie.gebruikers","zekerheid.onbekend","kanaal.online","niveau.offline","noodproces.handmatig","gegevens.onzeker","regie.organisatie","afstemming.gezamenlijk","publiek.dienst","herstel.niet"]}},{id:"hoogwater",label:"High water and flooding",desc:`Explore decisions about high water, residents’ exposure and access for assistance. The scenario options are fictional and do not replace current warnings.

Source: [Delta Programme – Flood protection](https://www.deltaprogramma.nl/themas/waterveiligheid).`,categories:[{id:"water",label:"Water conditions",desc:"The source and visible state of the water in the exercise area.",factors:[{id:"bron",label:"Dominant water source",desc:"Where does the water in this fictional situation mainly come from?",values:[["rivier","High river discharge"],["kust","High sea level"],["regen","Extreme rainfall"]]},{id:"beeld",label:"Visible effect",desc:"What observable consequences are there at present?",values:[["droog","Area still dry"],["straat","Streets flooded"],["woning","Buildings flooded"]]},{id:"verloop",label:"Change in water conditions",desc:"What change is known from observations or forecasts?",values:[["stijgend","Expected to rise"],["stabiel","Stable for now"],["dalend","Observed to be receding"]]}]},{id:"omgeving",label:"Area and exposure",desc:"The setting determines the nature of the potential societal consequences.",factors:[{id:"gebied",label:"Type of area",desc:"What area is the focus of the exercise?",values:[["stad","Densely built-up neighbourhood"],["dorp","Rural village"],["knooppunt","Essential facilities"]]},{id:"inwoners",label:"Potentially affected residents",desc:"How large is the group that may need assistance or information?",values:[["beperkt","A few households"],["wijk","A neighbourhood or village"],["regio","Several municipalities"]]},{id:"zorgvraag",label:"Specific care needs",desc:"Which support needs require explicit coordination with care providers?",values:[["mobiliteit","People with limited mobility"],["zorg","Care facilities"],["verspreid","Home-care clients spread across the area"]]}]},{id:"bereikbaarheid",label:"Access and assistance",desc:"Actual access routes constrain how assistance can arrive.",factors:[{id:"wegen",label:"Road access to the area",desc:"Are access roads available to vehicles?",values:[["open","All access roads passable"],["deels","Some access roads passable"],["dicht","All access roads closed"]]},{id:"aanvoer",label:"Arrival of assistance",desc:"How does assistance from outside reach the affected location?",values:[["direct","Via the usual access road"],["omweg","Via an alternative access road"],["nietweg","Not by road"]]},{id:"voorziening",label:"Availability of basic utilities",desc:"What effects on power, drinking water or communications must be considered?",values:[["normaal","Normally available"],["plaatselijk","Localised restrictions"],["meervoud","Multiple utilities restricted"]]}]},{id:"besluit",label:"Information and decisions",desc:"Warnings, shelter and cooperation involve decisions under uncertainty.",factors:[{id:"zekerheid",label:"Reliability of the situational picture",desc:"How certain is the information about water, roads and residents?",values:[["voorlopig","Preliminary reports"],["gedeeld","Shared but partly uncertain picture"],["bevestigd","Confirmed observations"]]},{id:"opvang",label:"Need for shelter",desc:"What demand for temporary support is expected?",values:[["thuis","Residents remain at home for now"],["lokaal","Temporary local shelter"],["regionaal","Coordination of regional shelter"]]},{id:"regie",label:"Inter-agency cooperation",desc:"Who shares a common picture for action?",values:[["gemeente","Municipality and water authority"],["regio","Regional crisis partners"],["grens","Several safety regions"]]}]}],exclusions:[["wegen.dicht","aanvoer.direct"],["wegen.dicht","aanvoer.omweg"]],template:`The dominant water source is {1}. The visible effect is {2}, while water conditions are expected to develop as {3}.
The area is {4}, and potential exposure includes {5}. The specific care needs concern {6}.
The access roads are {7}; assistance can arrive {8}. Basic utilities are {9}.
The situational picture is {10}. The need for shelter is {11}, while inter-agency cooperation involves {12}.`,prompt:"Write an English-language high-water scenario for a safety region using all selected values. Link the water source, the development of water conditions, care needs, access and utilities to public decisions about warnings and shelter. Show how confidence in the situational picture and cooperation among the water authority, municipality and region affect decisions. Distinguish forecasts from observations; do not assume precise water levels or damage without evidence. End with two exercise questions.",example:{label:"The detour to the village",desc:"<p>After a prolonged period of high water, streets in a rural village flood; the water level may rise further. Some access roads remain passable, but assistance must take a detour. The municipality and water authority share a still uncertain picture of the care needs of home-care clients.</p><p>With localised problems affecting utilities, temporary shelter is being considered. The question for the regional meeting is when nearby residents should be warned while the accessible area changes from hour to hour.</p>",choices:["bron.rivier","beeld.straat","verloop.stijgend","gebied.dorp","inwoners.wijk","zorgvraag.verspreid","wegen.deels","aanvoer.omweg","voorziening.plaatselijk","zekerheid.gedeeld","opvang.lokaal","regie.regio"]}},{id:"dijkdoorbraak",label:"Levee breach",desc:`Explore detection, uncertainty, relocation and continuity when a flood defence is damaged. This model does not allow a visible breach and an intact defence to be selected together.

Sources: [Delta Programme – Flood protection](https://www.deltaprogramma.nl/themas/waterveiligheid) and [Rijkswaterstaat – Protection from water](https://www.rijkswaterstaat.nl/water/waterbeheer/bescherming-tegen-het-water).`,categories:[{id:"kering",label:"Flood defence and observations",desc:"Make the physical situation and the level of confirmation explicit.",factors:[{id:"toestand",label:"Condition of the flood defence",desc:"What condition is established as the starting point for this exercise?",values:[["intact","Flood defence intact"],["schade","Damage without a breach"],["door","Flood defence breached"]]},{id:"bres",label:"Observed breach",desc:"What is actually known about any opening in the flood defence?",values:[["geen","No breach established"],["onzeker","Report not yet confirmed"],["bevestigd","Breach confirmed"]]},{id:"belasting",label:"Water pressure",desc:"What external pressure on the flood defence is expected in the exercise?",values:[["rivier","High river discharge"],["kust","High coastal water level"],["combinatie","Combined water pressure and rainfall"]]}]},{id:"gebied",label:"Area and time",desc:"Geographical context and available preparation time.",factors:[{id:"omgeving",label:"Area behind the flood defence",desc:"What type of area might be affected?",values:[["woonwijk","Residential neighbourhood"],["polder","Rural polder"],["bedrijven","Industrial estate"]]},{id:"tijd",label:"Time for measures",desc:"How much time does the exercise allow for public decision-making?",values:[["vooraf","Time to prepare"],["kort","Short response time"],["direct","Immediate decisions required"]]},{id:"blootstelling",label:"People behind the flood defence",desc:"Which group may need warning or support?",values:[["verspreid","Dispersed households"],["wijk","Densely populated community"],["zorg","Care facilities in the area"]]}]},{id:"gevolgen",label:"Societal consequences",desc:"Options for relocation and basic utilities, without prescribing a particular measure.",factors:[{id:"verplaatsing",label:"Relocation needs",desc:"What decision concerning residents is at issue?",values:[["blijven","Assess whether staying put is safe"],["gefaseerd","Consider phased relocation"],["snel","Prepare rapid relocation"]]},{id:"voorzieningen",label:"Basic utilities",desc:"How do power, drinking water and communications function in the scenario?",values:[["normaal","Normally available"],["deels","Locally restricted"],["uitval","Multiple utilities unavailable"]]},{id:"opvang",label:"Shelter capacity",desc:"What preparatory shelter options are available?",values:[["lokaal","Local facilities"],["regionaal","Regionally agreed shelter"],["onbekend","Capacity still being assessed"]]}]},{id:"regie",label:"Coordination and knowledge",desc:"Verification of observations and coordination between water authorities and public officials.",factors:[{id:"meting",label:"Situational picture",desc:"What information has been independently confirmed?",values:[["meldingen","Individual reports"],["gedeeld","Shared preliminary picture"],["bevestigd","Confirmed measurements"]]},{id:"afstemming",label:"Coordination among partners",desc:"Where do the relevant organisations make decisions together?",values:[["beheerder","Water authority and municipality"],["regio","Safety region and water partners"],["meerdere","Several regions and water authorities"]]},{id:"bericht",label:"Public communication",desc:"What can responsibly be shared based on the current picture?",values:[["waakzaam","Explain the uncertainty"],["voorbereiden","Prepare residents for measures"],["handelen","Inform residents about a current decision"]]}]}],exclusions:[["toestand.intact","bres.bevestigd"],["toestand.door","bres.geen"],["toestand.schade","bres.bevestigd"]],template:`The condition of the flood defence is {1}. Regarding a possible breach, {2}; water pressure is driven by {3}.
Behind the flood defence lies an area of the type {4}. The time available for measures is {5}; the potentially affected group consists of {6}.
The relocation decision concerns {7}. Basic utilities are {8} and shelter capacity is {9}.
The situational picture consists of {10}; coordination among partners takes place through {11}. Public communication is {12}.`,prompt:"Create a realistic English-language exercise scenario about a damaged or breached levee using all selected values. Describe the pressure on the flood defence, what has been confirmed about a breach, who lives behind it and how much time remains for decisions. Link verification and coordination to decisions about warning, relocation, shelter and basic utilities. Do not invent precise forecasts or instructions for work on the flood defence. End with two reflection questions for decision-makers.",example:{label:"An unconfirmed report near the polder",desc:"<p>After high river discharge, damage is reported at a flood defence beside a rural polder, but a breach has not yet been confirmed. Dispersed households have little time to prepare. The municipality and water authority share individual reports while shelter capacity is still being assessed.</p><p>The safety region considers phased relocation. It must decide what it can already tell residents about the uncertain condition of the flood defence without presenting a breach as an established fact.</p>",choices:["toestand.schade","bres.onzeker","belasting.rivier","omgeving.polder","tijd.kort","blootstelling.verspreid","verplaatsing.gefaseerd","voorzieningen.normaal","opvang.onbekend","meting.meldingen","afstemming.regio","bericht.waakzaam"]}},{id:"natuurbrand",label:"Wildfire",desc:`Use wildfire to explore the situational picture, smoke, public access and protection of people. This model does not forecast how a fire will spread.

Source: [NIPV – Wildfire research](https://nipv.nl/onderzoek/natuurbranden/).`,categories:[{id:"brand",label:"Fire and landscape",desc:"The landscape and current fire status for the exercise.",factors:[{id:"terrein",label:"Type of natural area",desc:"What landscape shapes the possible effects on people using the area?",values:[["bos","Wooded area"],["heide","Heathland"],["duin","Dune landscape"]]},{id:"status",label:"Fire status",desc:"Is there already a fire in the area under consideration?",values:[["dreiging","No fire in this area yet"],["lokaal","Localised fire"],["meervoud","Fires at several locations"]]},{id:"omstandigheden",label:"Conditions in the area",desc:"What weather and terrain conditions influence the situational picture?",values:[["droog","Dry and warm"],["wind","Strong winds"],["wisselend","Variable conditions"]]}]},{id:"omgeving",label:"Surroundings and smoke",desc:"Smoke and people present can call for different decisions.",factors:[{id:"rook",label:"Smoke from this fire",desc:"What smoke from the fire in this area has been observed?",values:[["geen","No smoke from this fire"],["plaatselijk","Localised smoke"],["wijd","Smoke in several residential communities"]]},{id:"mensen",label:"People present",desc:"Who in the area might be affected by the situation?",values:[["weinig","Few visitors"],["recreanten","Many recreational visitors"],["woningen","Residents nearby as well"]]},{id:"omgeving",label:"Activities at the edge of the area",desc:"Which community activities may face disruption or need information?",values:[["recreatie","Recreational facilities"],["wonen","Residential neighbourhoods"],["zorg","Care and accommodation facilities"]]}]},{id:"publiek",label:"Public access",desc:"Distinguish formal closures from the options actually available to the public.",factors:[{id:"afsluiting",label:"Public closure",desc:"What access restrictions apply to the public?",values:[["open","No closure"],["deels","Part of the area closed"],["dicht","Entire area closed to the public"]]},{id:"toegang",label:"Visitor access",desc:"How can visitors use the area during the exercise?",values:[["vrij","Unrestricted access throughout the area"],["geleid","Guided public access only"],["geen","No public access"]]},{id:"opvang",label:"Support for visitors",desc:"How are recreational visitors and residents supported or informed?",values:[["lokaal","Contact through site management"],["gemeente","Municipal support"],["regionaal","Regionally coordinated support"]]}]},{id:"regie",label:"Cooperation and recovery",desc:"A shared picture and appropriate follow-up help guide decisions.",factors:[{id:"beeld",label:"Confidence in the situational picture",desc:"How complete is the information about smoke and effects on the surrounding area?",values:[["eerste","Initial reports"],["gedeeld","Shared picture with uncertainties"],["bevestigd","Observations confirmed"]]},{id:"partners",label:"Organisations involved",desc:"Who must work together to provide a coherent public response?",values:[["beheer","Site manager and municipality"],["regio","Safety region and site management"],["grens","Several regions and site managers"]]},{id:"nazorg",label:"Recovery needs",desc:"What needs attention once the immediate pressure subsides?",values:[["toegang","Reopening the area"],["gezondheid","Explaining smoke and health effects"],["omgeving","Environmental recovery and evaluation"]]}]}],exclusions:[["status.dreiging","rook.plaatselijk"],["status.dreiging","rook.wijd"],["afsluiting.dicht","toegang.vrij"],["afsluiting.dicht","toegang.geleid"],["afsluiting.deels","toegang.vrij"]],template:`The area is {1}, where the fire status is {2}. Conditions on site are {3}.
Smoke from this fire is {4}. The people present in the area are {5}; at its edge are {6}.
The public closure is {7}, with {8} available to visitors. Support for those affected consists of {9}.
Confidence in the situational picture is {10}; the organisations involved are {11}. When the immediate pressure subsides, attention turns to {12}.`,prompt:"Write an English-language scenario for a safety region about a wildfire or the threat of one. Use all selected values concerning the landscape, weather conditions, fire status, smoke, visitors and activities around the area. Describe decisions concerning public access, support, uncertainty in the situational picture, cooperation and follow-up. Avoid precise predictions of fire spread and operational firefighting instructions. End with two exercise questions.",example:{label:"Smoke near the heathland",desc:"<p>A localised fire starts in dry heathland while many recreational visitors are present. Localised smoke is reported and part of the area is closed; guided public access remains possible in another part. Recreational facilities ask for one reliable situational picture.</p><p>The site manager and safety region coordinate municipal support for visitors. While initial reports are still incomplete, they also discuss how to prepare carefully for eventual reopening and communication about smoke.</p>",choices:["terrein.heide","status.lokaal","omstandigheden.droog","rook.plaatselijk","mensen.recreanten","omgeving.recreatie","afsluiting.deels","toegang.geleid","opvang.gemeente","beeld.eerste","partners.regio","nazorg.toegang"]}},{id:"demonstraties",label:"Demonstrations and public order",desc:"Explore peaceful demonstrations by, for example, farmers or students, or a protest outside an embassy. Participants’ identities do not imply a threat; the right to demonstrate and proportionate decisions come first.",categories:[{id:"bijeenkomst",label:"Purpose and format",desc:"The message and format are selected separately; groups must not be treated as risk profiles.",factors:[{id:"thema",label:"Demonstration context",desc:"What example makes the exercise concrete without stereotyping participants?",values:[["landbouw","Farmers discussing agricultural policy"],["studie","Students discussing education policy"],["diplomatie","Demonstration outside an embassy"]]},{id:"vorm",label:"Gathering format",desc:"Is movement part of the event?",values:[["statisch","Stationary gathering"],["mars","March"],["combinatie","Gathering followed by a march"]]},{id:"fase",label:"Stage of public decision-making",desc:"At what point in the public debate does the gathering take place?",values:[["voorstel","A proposal is being discussed"],["besluit","After an announced decision"],["evaluatie","During a policy evaluation"]]}]},{id:"ruimte",label:"Public space",desc:"The setting and planned route determine where interests intersect.",factors:[{id:"locatie",label:"Setting",desc:"What type of setting is relevant to exercising the right to demonstrate?",values:[["plein","City square"],["campus","Campus and surrounding area"],["diplomatiek","Neighbourhood with diplomatic premises"]]},{id:"route",label:"Movement of the gathering",desc:"What movement is planned in this exercise scenario?",values:[["geen","No movement"],["afgesproken","Previously discussed walking route"],["onbekend","Movement planned, route not yet known"]]},{id:"bereikbaarheid",label:"Access to the surrounding area",desc:"What effects on normal travel are known in advance?",values:[["normaal","Usual routes accessible"],["omleiding","Temporary diversions"],["onzeker","Access not yet known"]]}]},{id:"afstemming",label:"Coordination",desc:"Attendance and contact with organisers shape information provision, not participants’ rights.",factors:[{id:"opkomst",label:"Expected attendance",desc:"Approximately how many participants are expected?",values:[["klein","Dozens"],["middel","Hundreds"],["groot","Thousands"]]},{id:"contact",label:"Contact with organisers",desc:"What opportunities are there to coordinate?",values:[["bereikbaar","Contact persons reachable"],["los","Informally organised collective"],["onbekend","No contact established yet"]]},{id:"tijd",label:"Duration of the gathering",desc:"How long is the public space scheduled to be in use?",values:[["kort","Several hours"],["dag","Part of a day"],["lang","Several parts of a day"]]}]},{id:"rechten",label:"Rights and communication",desc:"Record the trade-offs without judging participants by identity.",factors:[{id:"kennisgeving",label:"Notification status",desc:"What contact has there been with the competent authority about the intended demonstration?",values:[["ontvangen","Notification received"],["laat","Became known at short notice"],["onzeker","Status still unclear"]]},{id:"belang",label:"Main consideration",desc:"What other public interest needs attention alongside the right to demonstrate?",values:[["toegang","Access for local residents"],["hulp","Access for emergency services"],["dialoog","Constructive dialogue among parties"]]},{id:"publiek",label:"Communication with local residents",desc:"What information about the event and access has been prepared?",values:[["lokaal","Local information"],["breed","Widely coordinated information"],["voorlopig","Preliminary information noting uncertainties"]]}]}],exclusions:[["vorm.statisch","route.afgesproken"],["vorm.statisch","route.onbekend"],["vorm.mars","route.geen"],["vorm.combinatie","route.geen"]],template:`The context of the demonstration is {1} and its format is {2}. It takes place at the stage of public decision-making described as {3}.
The gathering takes place at {4}. Movement is {5}, while access to the surrounding area is {6}.
Expected attendance is {7}. Contact with organisers is {8} and the planned duration is {9}.
Notification status is {10}. Alongside the right to demonstrate, {11} needs attention; local residents receive {12}.`,prompt:"Write a balanced English-language scenario about a peaceful demonstration using all selected values. Describe its purpose, the stage of decision-making, format, route, expected attendance and notification. Show how the right to demonstrate, contact with organisers, access for local residents and honest public communication are weighed against one another. Do not equate any group with a threat, invent criminal conduct or offer tactical guidance. End with two questions about proportionality.",example:{label:"A student march through the city",desc:"<p>After an announced education-policy decision, hundreds of students plan to march from the campus to the city square. Their contact persons have discussed a walking route for part of the day; temporary diversions will be needed. Notification has been received.</p><p>The municipality ensures that local residents know in good time which routes will remain accessible. The discussion centres on both the right to demonstrate and access to the neighbourhood. Organisers can communicate any changes directly.</p>",choices:["thema.studie","vorm.mars","fase.besluit","locatie.campus","route.afgesproken","bereikbaarheid.omleiding","opkomst.middel","contact.bereikbaar","tijd.dag","kennisgeving.ontvangen","belang.toegang","publiek.lokaal"]}},{id:"publieke-gebouwen",label:"Safety in public buildings",desc:"A governance-focused kit about access, service delivery and visitor care in public buildings. Explicitly select whether the building is open; do not describe vulnerabilities or ways to bypass safeguards.",categories:[{id:"gebouw",label:"Building and use",desc:"Which public function and opening status are central?",factors:[{id:"functie",label:"Building function",desc:"What service or function are visitors coming to use?",values:[["gemeente","Town hall"],["cultuur","Library or museum"],["onderwijs","Educational building"]]},{id:"opening",label:"Open to the public",desc:"How accessible is the building to the public at present?",values:[["open","Open to the public"],["beperkt","Partly open"],["gesloten","Completely closed to the public"]]},{id:"gebruik",label:"Type of use",desc:"What activity makes the space in question important right now?",values:[["loket","Public services"],["bijeenkomst","Scheduled gathering"],["dagelijks","Everyday education or cultural activities"]]}]},{id:"bezoekers",label:"Visitors and surroundings",desc:"Occupancy and visitor arrangements together shape hospitality needs.",factors:[{id:"bezoek",label:"Visitor admission",desc:"Under what conditions may visitors enter?",values:[["vrij","Walk-in access"],["afspraak","By appointment only"],["geen","No public admitted"]]},{id:"drukte",label:"Occupancy",desc:"How many people are expected in the building?",values:[["laag","Low occupancy"],["middel","Moderate occupancy"],["hoog","High occupancy"]]},{id:"behoefte",label:"Accessibility needs",desc:"Which visitors need additional support when arrangements change?",values:[["taal","Multilingual explanation"],["digitaal","Help through non-digital channels"],["mobiliteit","Accessible assistance"]]}]},{id:"dienst",label:"Service delivery and entrance",desc:"How are services and physical public entrances related?",factors:[{id:"service",label:"Service delivery",desc:"How is the public function kept available?",values:[["normaal","Normal service delivery"],["beperkt","Limited service delivery"],["online","Primarily remote service delivery"]]},{id:"entree",label:"Public entrances",desc:"To what extent are entrances open to visitors?",values:[["open","All public entrances open"],["deels","One public entrance open"],["dicht","All public entrances closed"]]},{id:"verstoring",label:"Effect on the service",desc:"What effect does a visitor notice from the change?",values:[["wachttijd","Longer wait"],["verplaatst","Appointment rescheduled"],["alternatief","Different form of service delivery"]]}]},{id:"regie",label:"Continuity and aftercare",desc:"Users’ needs remain visible even when access is restricted.",factors:[{id:"beheer",label:"Coordination between building and service",desc:"How do building management and the service provider make decisions together?",values:[["direct","Direct contact"],["team","Joint meeting"],["keten","Meeting with external partners"]]},{id:"alternatief",label:"Alternative for visitors",desc:"How can people unable to enter still access an essential service?",values:[["afspraak","New appointment"],["locatie","Alternative location"],["afstand","Remote assistance"]]},{id:"bericht",label:"Information for the public",desc:"When do visitors receive an explanation about changed access?",values:[["vooraf","In advance through familiar channels"],["terplekke","On arrival"],["persoonlijk","Personally for an existing appointment"]]}]}],exclusions:[["opening.gesloten","bezoek.vrij"],["opening.gesloten","entree.open"],["opening.gesloten","entree.deels"],["bezoek.vrij","entree.dicht"],["bezoek.geen","entree.open"]],template:`The building serves as {1} and is {2} to the public. The space is used for {3}.
Visitors are admitted by {4}, with {5}. Visitors’ accessibility needs include {6}.
Service delivery is {7} and the public entrances are {8}. Visitors experience {9} as a result.
Building management and the service provider coordinate through {10}. The alternative for visitors is {11}; they receive information {12}.`,prompt:"Create an English-language scenario about continuity and visitor care in a public building. Use all selected values concerning use, opening status, occupancy, accessibility needs, service disruption and alternative service delivery. Link decisions by building management and the service provider to clear information and the effects on visitors. Do not describe technical or physical vulnerabilities. End with two questions for the organisation.",example:{label:"The town hall remains accessible",desc:"<p>A town hall receives visitors to its public service desk by appointment only, while one entrance remains open. Occupancy is moderate and service delivery is temporarily limited. Residents who struggle with digital services in particular face longer waits.</p><p>Building management and the service agree on an alternative at a joint meeting: anyone who cannot be seen receives a new appointment personally. This keeps essential services accessible without assuming that everyone can manage online.</p>",choices:["functie.gemeente","opening.beperkt","gebruik.loket","bezoek.afspraak","drukte.middel","behoefte.digitaal","service.beperkt","entree.deels","verstoring.wachttijd","beheer.team","alternatief.afspraak","bericht.persoonlijk"]}},{id:"religieuze-centra",label:"Safety at religious centres",desc:"An inclusive exercise kit about hospitality, gatherings and care for visitors at religious centres. Faith or community affiliation is not treated as a risk.",categories:[{id:"bijeenkomst",label:"Gathering and visitors",desc:"The activity determines who is welcome and how many people are expected.",factors:[{id:"activiteit",label:"Activity",desc:"What activity takes place in the building?",values:[["publiek","Publicly accessible service"],["besloten","Private gathering"],["geen","No group gathering; individual visits possible"]]},{id:"bezoekers",label:"Who may attend",desc:"To whom is the gathering open?",values:[["iedereen","Public welcome"],["gasten","Invitees only"],["niemand","No public admitted"]]},{id:"ritme",label:"Timing of the gathering",desc:"When and with what preparation do people gather?",values:[["regulier","Regular gathering"],["feestdag","Busy holiday"],["bijzonder","Special community gathering"]]}]},{id:"omgeving",label:"Setting and attendance",desc:"The relationship with the surrounding area and the scale of the gathering.",factors:[{id:"plek",label:"Centre surroundings",desc:"Where is the building relative to everyday visitor flows?",values:[["buurt","Residential neighbourhood"],["centrum","City centre"],["dorp","Village centre"]]},{id:"drukte",label:"Expected attendance",desc:"How many visitors will be present at the same time?",values:[["klein","Small group"],["middel","Medium-sized group"],["groot","Busy gathering"]]},{id:"mobiliteit",label:"Access for visitors",desc:"What mode of arrival needs attention for the gathering?",values:[["lopen","Mainly on foot"],["vervoer","Mix of public transport and cars"],["ondersteuning","Additional accessible transport needed"]]}]},{id:"gastvrijheid",label:"Hospitality and communication",desc:"Public access and communication are organised with visitors’ needs in mind.",factors:[{id:"toegang",label:"Access to the centre",desc:"How is visitor access arranged?",values:[["open","Walk-in access"],["uitnodiging","By invitation only"],["dicht","No visitor access"]]},{id:"communicatie",label:"Contact with the surrounding area",desc:"How is relevant information shared with those involved?",values:[["intern","Through the community"],["buurt","With local residents as well"],["breed","Through public channels as well"]]},{id:"welkom",label:"On-site support",desc:"How are people with different needs welcomed?",values:[["vrijwilligers","Volunteers as points of contact"],["meertalig","Multilingual assistance"],["zorg","Support for visitors with reduced mobility"]]}]},{id:"samenwerking",label:"Cooperation and aftercare",desc:"Decisions are made with the community and keep accessibility central.",factors:[{id:"regie",label:"Decision-making",desc:"Who decides how to adapt reception and communication?",values:[["gemeenschap","Community organisation"],["buurt","Together with neighbourhood organisations"],["publiek","Together with relevant public partners"]]},{id:"zorg",label:"Additional attention",desc:"What issue deserves extra attention after a busy gathering?",values:[["toegang","Accessibility of participation"],["contact","Contact with local residents"],["nazorg","Aftercare for visitors"]]},{id:"terugkoppeling",label:"Evaluation",desc:"How are visitors’ and volunteers’ experiences gathered?",values:[["gesprek","Discussion afterwards"],["gemeenschap","Feedback within the community"],["samen","Joint evaluation"]]}]}],exclusions:[["activiteit.publiek","bezoekers.niemand"],["activiteit.publiek","toegang.dicht"],["bezoekers.iedereen","toegang.dicht"]],template:`The activity at the religious centre is {1}. Attendance is {2} and the timing of the gathering is {3}.
The centre is located in {4} and expects {5}. Visitor access involves {6}.
Access to the centre is {7}; communication reaches {8}. Reception includes {9}.
Decision-making involves {10}, with particular attention to {11}. Visitors’ and volunteers’ experiences are collected through {12}.`,prompt:"Write a respectful English-language scenario for a religious centre using all selected values. Link the timing and size of the gathering, transport, reception and open access to hospitality, cooperation with the community and considerate communication with local residents. State who makes decisions and how visitors’ experiences are evaluated. Do not infer threats from religion or mention vulnerabilities or security details. End with two reflection questions.",example:{label:"A busy gathering in the neighbourhood",desc:"<p>A publicly accessible holiday service brings many visitors to a centre in a residential neighbourhood. Many people arrive by transport from the surrounding area. The organisation maintains walk-in access and informs local residents about the expected crowds.</p><p>Volunteers welcome visitors. The community discusses with the neighbourhood how everyone can participate without placing unnecessary pressure on access. Afterwards, visitors and volunteers share their experiences in a discussion.</p>",choices:["activiteit.publiek","bezoekers.iedereen","ritme.feestdag","plek.buurt","drukte.groot","mobiliteit.vervoer","toegang.open","communicatie.buurt","welkom.vrijwilligers","regie.buurt","zorg.contact","terugkoppeling.gesprek"]}},{id:"havencontinuiteit",label:"Port continuity",desc:"Explore how disruptions to port logistics affect service delivery and partner organisations. Capacity and throughput describe only the fictional terminal, including when it processes passengers rather than freight; no security details.",categories:[{id:"haven",label:"Port function",desc:"The terminal type and current operations in the exercise.",factors:[{id:"functie",label:"Port function",desc:"What is the function of the fictional terminal under consideration?",values:[["container","Container handling"],["veer","Ferry service"],["gemengd","Mixed logistics"]]},{id:"afhandeling",label:"Terminal operations",desc:"Can the terminal process freight and passengers?",values:[["normaal","Normal operations"],["beperkt","Limited operations"],["stil","Operations suspended"]]},{id:"tijd",label:"Expected duration of disruption",desc:"How long does the organisation expect the terminal to be affected?",values:[["kort","Several hours"],["dag","One day"],["lang","Several days"]]}]},{id:"keten",label:"Supply chain and shipping",desc:"Dependencies outside the terminal may persist even when its operations are limited.",factors:[{id:"scheepvaart",label:"Shipping in the port",desc:"What traffic conditions apply to the wider port, beyond this terminal?",values:[["normaal","Normal traffic"],["beperkt","Limited traffic"],["omgeleid","Traffic being diverted"]]},{id:"druk",label:"Pressure on partner organisations",desc:"How much coordination is needed with carriers and authorities?",values:[["laag","Limited"],["middel","Noticeable"],["hoog","High"]]},{id:"achterland",label:"Hinterland connections",desc:"What is known about transport beyond the terminal?",values:[["normaal","Normally available"],["beperkt","Limited availability"],["onzeker","Capacity still unclear"]]}]},{id:"capaciteit",label:"Terminal capacity",desc:"Show capacity and actual flows of freight or passengers separately.",factors:[{id:"capaciteit",label:"Terminal processing capacity",desc:"How much of the normal processing capacity is available?",values:[["normaal","Fully available"],["beperkt","Partially available"],["geen","No processing capacity"]]},{id:"stroom",label:"Flow through the terminal",desc:"What freight or passenger processing still takes place at this specific terminal?",values:[["normaal","Normal flow"],["beperkt","Limited flow"],["geen","No flow"]]},{id:"bezetting",label:"Available staff",desc:"How much of the usual workforce can support the service?",values:[["normaal","Normal staffing"],["beperkt","Reduced staffing"],["wisselend","Variable staffing"]]}]},{id:"regie",label:"Supply-chain coordination and recovery",desc:"Coordinate the terminal’s effects with public service needs and partners.",factors:[{id:"prioriteit",label:"Priority service",desc:"Which interest receives particular attention in decisions?",values:[["reiziger","Continuity for passengers"],["levering","Continuity of deliveries"],["veiligheid","Care for staff and the surrounding area"]]},{id:"afstemming",label:"Shared situational picture",desc:"With which parties is the terminal’s status shared?",values:[["terminal","Terminal and port authority"],["keten","Logistics partners"],["overheid","Supply-chain partners and government"]]},{id:"informatie",label:"Explanation to those affected",desc:"How are plans and uncertainties communicated?",values:[["gericht","Targeted updates for customers"],["breed","Broad public communication"],["voorlopig","Preliminary status noting uncertainties"]]}]}],exclusions:[["afhandeling.normaal","capaciteit.geen"],["afhandeling.stil","stroom.normaal"],["afhandeling.stil","stroom.beperkt"],["capaciteit.geen","stroom.normaal"],["capaciteit.geen","stroom.beperkt"]],template:`The terminal under consideration serves as {1}. Operations are {2}, for an expected duration of {3}.
For shipping in the port as a whole, conditions are {4}. Pressure on partner organisations is {5}; hinterland connections have {6}.
The terminal’s processing capacity is {7}, while the actual flow through the terminal is {8}. Staffing is {9}.
The service priority is {10}. The shared situational picture includes {11}, and those affected receive {12}.`,prompt:"Write an English-language continuity scenario for a fictional port terminal. Show how duration, terminal function, available staff, throughput and hinterland connections affect decisions for passengers or deliveries. Make explicit what applies only to the terminal and what applies to the entire port. Do not describe access routes, vulnerabilities or security procedures. End with two questions about cooperation and recovery.",example:{label:"A terminal scales back",desc:"<p>A container terminal expects to handle only limited traffic for one day, while shipping elsewhere in the port continues normally. Terminal staffing varies and hinterland connections are limited. As a result, throughput falls and supply-chain partners seek clear expectations.</p><p>The port authority, carriers and government coordinate which deliveries take priority. In targeted updates, they explain why the effects on this terminal do not mean that the whole port has stopped operating.</p>",choices:["functie.container","afhandeling.beperkt","tijd.dag","scheepvaart.normaal","druk.hoog","achterland.beperkt","capaciteit.beperkt","stroom.beperkt","bezetting.wisselend","prioriteit.levering","afstemming.overheid","informatie.gericht"]}},{id:"luchthavencontinuiteit",label:"Airport continuity",desc:"An exercise kit about flight operations, passenger care and communication at a fictional airport. In this model, if all operational runways are closed, no take-offs or landings take place.",categories:[{id:"vluchten",label:"Airport and flights",desc:"Airport type and current take-offs and landings.",factors:[{id:"functie",label:"Airport function",desc:"What is the scale and function of the fictional airport?",values:[["regionaal","Regional airport"],["internationaal","International airport"],["gemengd","Mixed-use airport"]]},{id:"operatie",label:"Take-offs and landings",desc:"What flight operations are actually taking place in the exercise?",values:[["normaal","On the normal schedule"],["beperkt","Limited number of flights"],["stil","No take-offs or landings"]]},{id:"tijd",label:"Expected duration",desc:"How long is the uncertainty about the situation expected to last?",values:[["kort","Several hours"],["dag","Part of a day"],["lang","More than one day"]]}]},{id:"infrastructuur",label:"Available infrastructure",desc:"Runways and the terminal can be restricted independently.",factors:[{id:"banen",label:"Operational runways",desc:"Are runways available for flights?",values:[["open","All runways available"],["deels","Some available"],["dicht","All runways closed"]]},{id:"terminal",label:"Passenger terminal",desc:"Is the passenger terminal open?",values:[["open","Fully open"],["deels","Partly open"],["dicht","Fully closed"]]},{id:"verbinding",label:"Transport to and from the airport",desc:"What options are available to travellers in the region?",values:[["normaal","Normal transport"],["beperkt","Limited transport"],["onzeker","Alternatives being investigated"]]}]},{id:"reizigers",label:"Travellers and information",desc:"What services and information do travellers receive?",factors:[{id:"verwerking",label:"Passenger processing in the terminal",desc:"To what extent are travellers being processed in the terminal?",values:[["normaal","Normal"],["beperkt","Limited"],["stil","Stopped"]]},{id:"informatie",label:"Information for travellers",desc:"How quickly can those involved share an up-to-date picture?",values:[["tijdig","Timely joint updates"],["traag","Delayed updates"],["onzeker","Uncertain picture"]]},{id:"opvang",label:"Passenger care",desc:"What support has been arranged for stranded or delayed travellers?",values:[["terplekke","Information on site"],["vervoer","Help finding alternative transport"],["opvang","Temporary shelter being coordinated"]]}]},{id:"regie",label:"Decisions with partners",desc:"An airport also depends on carriers, government and regional services.",factors:[{id:"partners",label:"Partners involved",desc:"Who develops a shared picture of the situation?",values:[["luchthaven","Airport and airlines"],["regionaal","Regional carriers as well"],["breed","Relevant authorities and care partners as well"]]},{id:"keuze",label:"Main consideration",desc:"What public interest faces time pressure?",values:[["reizigers","Care for travellers"],["vluchten","Prioritising flights"],["omgeving","Effects on the surrounding area"]]},{id:"herstel",label:"Recovery outlook",desc:"How certain is the return to the normal flight schedule?",values:[["onbekend","Still unknown"],["gefaseerd","Phased resumption planned"],["normaal","Normal operations restored"]]}]}],exclusions:[["banen.dicht","operatie.normaal"],["banen.dicht","operatie.beperkt"],["terminal.dicht","verwerking.normaal"],["terminal.dicht","verwerking.beperkt"]],template:`The fictional airport serves as {1}. Take-offs and landings are {2}, for an expected duration of {3}.
Operational runways are {4}; the passenger terminal is {5}. Transport to and from the airport is {6}.
Passenger processing in the terminal is {7}. Travellers receive {8}, and passenger care consists of {9}.
The partners involved include {10}. The main consideration is {11}, while the recovery outlook is {12}.`,prompt:"Create an English-language scenario about continuity and passenger care at a fictional airport using all selected values. Describe flight operations, the terminal, passenger processing and regional transport separately, and account for uncertainty about duration and the recovery outlook. Show how the airport, carriers and authorities support travellers and coordinate information. Avoid specific infrastructure vulnerabilities and technical security details. End with two questions about information for travellers.",example:{label:"Travellers await clarity",desc:"<p>An international airport expects to handle a limited number of flights for part of a day. Part of the terminal is out of use and travellers face delays. Regional transport can also carry fewer people, while updates from carriers arrive late.</p><p>The airport, airlines and regional carriers coordinate temporary shelter and alternative travel options. The return to a normal flight schedule remains uncertain, so care for travellers is central to deciding what information can already be shared.</p>",choices:["functie.internationaal","operatie.beperkt","tijd.dag","banen.deels","terminal.deels","verbinding.beperkt","verwerking.beperkt","informatie.traag","opvang.opvang","partners.regionaal","keuze.reizigers","herstel.onbekend"]}}],a={effectsPrompt:e,boxes:i};export{i as boxes,a as default,e as effectsPrompt};

